  "body": "## Result\n\n30004435 / OWR-17474-009: **unsolved, 5/5**, with an independent full scoped source/proof PASS.\n\nThe equality of the one-sided tails is known through entropy theory. The original request specifically asks for a probability-only proof without entropy; this packet does not resolve that unrestricted method request.\n\n## Scoped progress\n\nFive genuine turns prove finite Markov class/phase classification, finite hidden-Markov observable-law quotients with a finite word certificate, a uniformly overlapping summably continuous infinite-memory coupling criterion, finite-mean finitary coding transfer, and non-atomic conditional-mixing mixture classification. Explicit weak-limit, coding and binary irrational-rotation examples identify limits of those reductions.\n\nAll subclass assumptions and classical credit are retained. No bilateral-tail conclusion is inferred from mixing alone, and no original counterexample or novelty claim is made.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll210,974 author assertions replay byte-for-byte, with166 author manifest entries and four source PDF hashes verified. The independent audit checks every proof and adds9,334 exact controls. Both replay commands are portable standard-library Python and documented in README.md.\n\nThis draft preserves every frozen author/review byte, fresh-main ancestry and the final author WIP. Its diff is limited to this target folder and the target QUEUE status/turn cells. Raw sources and imported reports are excluded. No merge or release.\n",
